# Derived by hand from Semantics Appendix B (`@Flatten: fn $$a -> @$a` takes any dynamic of dynamics, an expression as well as a name), ch. 4 (a row reads its block's names) and ruling FV, as sem-ch07-flatten-call's transcript is for the same outer in the block: the row adopts the outer's inner at its build (the constant 0); the inc moves the outer at 1, so the flatten reads the constant 1 at 2; the swap moves it at 3 to the constant of `$b` (101) or of the row's `$v` (7), read at 4; never run.
test over_the_blocks_names

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    1: Ui.Button(label="swap")
    2/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x: 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click

tick 2
  changed:
    2/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x: 1")

tick 3
  in:
    1: click

tick 4
  changed:
    2/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x: 101")

